<title>USA: Gulfstream Aerospace edges up after IPO.</title>
<headline>Gulfstream Aerospace edges up after IPO.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of corporate jetmaker Gulfstream Aerospace Corp had only a small lift-off at the company's New York Stock Exchange market debut on Thursday.</p>
<p>The shares rose 1-1/2 to 25-1/2 and were the most active issue on the NYSE. They priced at $24 each, the high end of the estimated pricing range of $22 to $24.  </p>
<p>The company scored gains on its first day of trading even after heavily increasing the number of shares to be offered to 37 million from its initial estimate of 28 million.</p>
</text>
